DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhvvnn driver provides support for a Network Virtual Service Client
     (NetVSC), a virtual networking interface that relays device requests to
     the Virtual Service Provider (VSP) in the management operating system via
     the VMBus.

     NetVSC emulates an RNDIS 1.0 compliant device on top of a custom NVS pro‐
     tocol operating over the VMBus channel ring.

     Individual networking interfaces can be renamed by issuing a
     RReennaammee--VVMMNNeettwwoorrkkAAddaapptteerr PowerShell command in the management domain.  In
     order to enable sending and receiving of IEEE 802.1q (VLAN) frames, the
     virtual port needs to be put into _T_r_u_n_k mode with the
     SSeett--VVMMNNeettwwoorrkkAAddaapptteerrVVllaann command.

